t_British_Isles","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7609206M/The_Pagan_Religions_of_the_Ancient_British_Isles","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/395792-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Blackwell Publishing Limited"],"number_of_pages":424,"subtitle":"Their Nature and Legacy","covers":[395792],"lc_classifications":["BL980.G7H87 1993","BL980.G7 H87 1993"],"key":"/books/OL7609206M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL27813A","name":"Ronald Hutton"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["ia:paganreligionsan00hutt","bwb:9780631189466","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_037.bib.mrc:338796348:2187"],"title":"The Pagan Religions of the Ancient British Isles","identifiers":{"goodreads":["765665"],"librarything":["92674"]},"isbn_13":["9780631189466"],"isbn_10":["0631189467"],"publish_date":"November 1, 1993","works":[{"key":"/works/OL31763W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The human record in the British Isles goes back a very long way beyond the beginning of the islands themselves."},"lccn":["90027166"],"oclc_numbers":["30758682"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"This is the first survey of religious beliefs in the British Isles, from the Old Stone Age to the coming of Christianity, one of the least familiar but most extensive periods in Britain's history. Ronald Hutton draws upon a wealth of new data, much of it archaeological, that has transformed interpretation over the past decade. Giving more or less equal weight to all periods, from the Neolithic to the Middle Ages, he considers a fascinating range of evidence for Celtic and Romano-British paganism: from burial sites, cairns, megaliths and causeways, to carvings, figurines, jewellery, weapons, votive objects, literary texts and folklore.\" -- Back Cover."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"